[76.698564, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0mgcc -Wall -Wextra -pedantic /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain && for n in 0 1 2 3 4 5 10 20 50 90 93 94 100 200 500 1000 5000; do p=$(python3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c \"$n\"); c=$(/app/polyglot/cmain \"$n\"); if [ \"$p\" != \"$c\" ]; then echo \"mismatch at $n\"; echo \"py=$p\"; echo \"c =$c\"; exit 1; fi; done && echo 'all outputs match' && python3 --version && gcc --version | head -n 1\r\nall outputs match\r\nPython 3.12.3\r\ngcc (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0\r\n"]
[77.652768, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[80.949073, "o", "Created `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`.\r\n\r\nIt works as both:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython3 /app/polyglot/main.py.c 10\r\n# 55\r\n\r\ngcc /app/polyglot/main.py.c -o /app/polyglot/cmain\r\n/app/polyglot/cmain 10\r\n# 55\r\n```\r\n\r\nI tested it with both interpreters through larger values like `N=5000`; outputs match. The C side uses arbitrary-precision arithmetic, so it isn’t limited to 64-bit Fibonacci values.\r\n"]
